  "protocol": {
    "summary": "Same protocol as the stiffness test (Costi 2008 Table 1).",
    "how_to_simulate": [
      "Model a vertebra-disc-vertebra segment without posterior elements (keep ALL/PLL); fix the lower vertebra; rotation centre = disc centre",
      "Equilibrate under 0.4 MPa axial compressive stress (x disc area; paper assumed ~1500 mm2 -> ~600 N) at 37 C if the model is poroelastic",
      "Apply sinusoidal displacement in one DOF at a time: +-0.25 mm compression, +-0.6 mm A-P/lateral shear, +-2 deg flexion-extension, +-3 deg lateral bending, +-2 deg axial rotation, at 0.001, 0.01, 0.1 and 1 Hz (other DOF held)",
      "Compute the phase lag between input displacement and reaction force/moment (viscoelastic/poroelastic models only)"
    ],
    "subject_model": null,
    "notes": "Mean (95% CI); sd derived as CI/t*sqrt(n). Only meaningful for rate-dependent (viscoelastic/poroelastic) disc models."
